---
/* The site's contact surface, on every page including /404.
   Decided in issue #34: `mailto:` stays, and a LinkedIn link joins it. No
   contact form — see docs/content-architecture.md §1 for the reasoning and for
   the trigger that would reopen it.

   This is the repo's first component, so it sets the precedent: scoped <style>
   in the file, no token hard-coded, no new type role. */
import { EMAIL, LINKEDIN } from '../site';
---

{/* Nothing here enters, and two separate arguments say so should it ever be
    proposed again: the footer is on the first screen on /404, which rules it out
    on LCP grounds, and it is furniture that is simply present rather than
    information arriving. Both are recorded in docs/motion.md. */}
<footer class="t-spec">
  <a class="address" href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>
  {/* rel="me" pairs with the Person graph's sameAs on /. No target="_blank":
      it decides tab behaviour on the visitor's behalf and drags rel="noopener"
      in behind it. */}
  <a href={LINKEDIN} rel="me">LinkedIn</a>
</footer>

<style>
  /* Aligned to the same measure and gutter as every page's <main>, so the
     footer sits on the page's left edge rather than the viewport's. That
     measure is now the --measure-page token rather than 1600px written out
     here and again in the page — it was two copies of one number, and
     src/layout.ts composes `sizes` from the token as well.

     `width: 100%` for the reason spelled out in base.css: <body> is a flex
     column, and `margin-inline: auto` on a flex item beats `align-items:
     stretch`, so without it this shrink-to-fits and centres itself. */
  footer {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px 28px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--measure-page);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: calc(var(--rhythm) * 0.5) var(--gutter);
  }

  /* --muted arrives from .t-spec. It is 4.90:1 on the day ground and 5.01:1 on
     the night ground — computed from the oklab mixes in tokens.css, not eyeballed.
     --t-spec is 0.6875rem = 11px, so the WCAG large-text 3:1 exemption does not
     apply and 4.5:1 is the bar. NEVER --signal here: it is not a text colour. */
  a {
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  /* NO .address RULE. The address is set exactly like the LinkedIn link beside
     it, which means uppercase and --track-spec, because both are .t-spec and a
     type style that reads one way in one place and another way next to it is not
     a style. Reversed on owner review; the previous rule set this one line in
     lowercase at normal tracking, which made it a tenth type treatment on a site
     trying to hold six.

     The lowercase is not lost, it just is not the rendering: `text-transform`
     changes glyphs, never the DOM, so the `mailto:` still carries the real
     lowercase address from src/site.ts and so does the copied text.

     WHAT THIS ORPHANS: U+0061-007A was added to MONO_SPEC in
     scripts/dev/subset-fonts.mjs for this line and no other — every remaining
     mono role is uppercase, and unicode-range is matched POST-text-transform, so
     nothing on the site can now reach a lowercase mono glyph. That is 1,208 B of
     dead weight in a file on the LCP Path. Left in rather than regenerated here:
     the subset needs the upstream font sources, which are deliberately not
     committed, and 1,208 B is about 6 ms against a gate we are 200+ ms over.
     Drop the range at the next regeneration. */
</style>
